(text "XTAL - 32.768 kHz  |  ECS ECX-31B  |  ECS-.327-7-34B-TR  |  Pierce oscillator" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 14.00 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0b386bb5-3ef9-4f29-8eaa-c7c3af101ca1"))
(text "House-common passives: load caps 10 pF C0G 0603, Rext 0R jumper, Rf 1M (DNP). Typical use: RTC / LSE, low-power timers." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 19.30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "36878eb0-cefc-4ba2-aeea-afd0ce52dc3e"))
(text "DESIGN EQUATIONS - 32.768 kHz crystal, ECS-.327-7-34B-TR (ECS ECX-31B); refs: ST AN2867 / TI SZZA043 / TI SLAA322\nCrystal: CL = 7 pF, ESR max = 70 kohm\n  C0 ~1.5 pF and DL max 0.5 uW are typical tuning-fork values (verify on ECX-31B sheet). Uses: RTC / LSE, low-power timers\nLoad caps: C1 = C2 = 2*(CL - Cs), Cs = 2.0 pF (pin + trace, edit for your layout) = 10.0 pF -> 10 pF C0G 5% (house value)\n  Effective CL = C1*C2/(C1+C2) + Cs = 5 + 2.0 = 7.0 pF (+0.0 pF vs spec)\nPulling: S = C1m/(2*(C0+CL)^2) ~ 13.8 ppm/pF (C1m ~2 fF typ, assumed) ; 5% cap tol -> dCL +/-0.25 pF -> +/-3.5 ppm\nOscillation margin: gm_crit = 4*ESR*(2*pi*f)^2*(C0+CL)^2 = 0.858 uA/V\n  Gain margin >= 5 -> oscillator gm must exceed 4.29 uA/V (check MCU LSE drive setting)\nDrive level @ 1.0 Vpp on XOUT: DL = ESR*(2*pi*f*(C0+CL)*Vpp/(2*sqrt2))^2 = 0.03 uW vs 0.5 uW max -> OK\nDrive level @ 3.3 Vpp on XOUT: DL = ESR*(2*pi*f*(C0+CL)*Vpp/(2*sqrt2))^2 = 0.29 uW vs 0.5 uW max -> OK\nRext (series, XOUT side): start value 1/(2*pi*f*C2) = 485.70 kohm ; fitted 0R (house jumper) - populate only if DL exceeded,\n  then re-check gain margin with ESR -> ESR + Rext. Rf 1M (house) shown DNP: fit only if the oscillator has no internal feedback resistor.\nLayout: C1/C2 and crystal within ~5 mm of the pins, GND guard ring, no signals under the crystal, return C1/C2 to the oscillator GND pin." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 128.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6f3542c7-6975-499e-9963-77b397d507bd"))
